opam-version: "2.0"
synopsis: "Rocq proofs on random ellipsoid fitting and other theorems, with the library GaussianAnalysis"
description: """
A Rocq proof of the three main results of "The sharp SAT/UNSAT phase
transition in random ellipsoid fitting" (Misiakiewicz and Wen,
arXiv:2608.10184v1): the sharp ellipsoid fitting transition at
n/d^2 = 1/4, well-conditioned fits below it, and the balanced
positive-definite alternative, for n independent standard Gaussian points
of R^d. The statement is theories/MainStatement.v.

extension/ goes beyond Gaussian points: Theorem 1.2 of Koehler and Sohn
(arXiv:2608.27372v1), exact fitting for finite and countable mixtures of
product laws and for two dependent laws, the optimal condition number at
every fourth moment kappa > 1, robustness in total variation, and seven
theorems on samples translated by deterministic shifts. applications/
formalizes thirteen theorems of manuscripts of the OpenAI math collection,
among them the satisfiability threshold of random k-SAT and an exponential
lower bound on the PSD rank of the shifted matching matrices. library/ is
GaussianAnalysis, a Rocq library on Gaussian measures, Gaussian comparison
and concentration inequalities, and the linear algebra and probability
tools they need, written over an arbitrary realType in the style of
MathComp-Analysis.

The package has no install step: the four directories are used from a
clone, through the -Q lines of _CoqProject.
"""
maintainer: "Marc Lelarge <marc.lelarge@inria.fr>"
authors: ["Marc Lelarge"]
license: "MIT"
homepage: "https://github.com/LLM4Rocq/ellipsoid_fitting_rocq"
bug-reports: "https://github.com/LLM4Rocq/ellipsoid_fitting_rocq/issues"
dev-repo: "git+https://github.com/LLM4Rocq/ellipsoid_fitting_rocq.git"
build: [make "build" "ROCQ_SWITCH=" "JOBS=%{jobs}%"]
depends: [
  "rocq-core" {>= "9.1" & < "9.2~"}
  "rocq-stdlib"
  "rocq-hierarchy-builder" {>= "1.10.3"}
  "rocq-mathcomp-ssreflect" {= "2.6.0"}
  "rocq-mathcomp-fingroup" {= "2.6.0"}
  "rocq-mathcomp-algebra" {= "2.6.0"}
  "rocq-mathcomp-finmap" {>= "2.2.4"}
  "rocq-mathcomp-classical" {= "1.16.0"}
  "rocq-mathcomp-reals" {= "1.16.0"}
  "rocq-mathcomp-reals-stdlib" {= "1.16.0"}
  "rocq-mathcomp-analysis" {= "1.16.0"}
  "rocq-mathcomp-analysis-stdlib" {= "1.16.0"}
]
